  "description": "Opposite-ends and same-direction pointers with the invariant behind every move: sorted pair sum, container with most water, palindromes, 3Sum dedup, in-place compaction, Dutch national flag and merging from the back.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">45 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Pattern primer</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">SDE-1 core</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Two pointers</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Two indexes walk the same array and, at every step, one of them moves because we can <b>prove</b> that the elements it leaves behind are no longer useful. Opposite ends solve pair sums, containers and palindromes; same-direction pointers compact, partition and merge in place. O(n) time, O(1) extra space.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Before this page:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-arrays-hashing\">Arrays and hashing</a> (two-sum with a map). <b>Next:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-sliding-window\">Sliding window</a> (two pointers that bound a window) and <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-linked-list\">Linked lists</a> (fast and slow pointers).</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Go deeper:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-sliding-window-variants\">Sliding window variants: at most K, exactly K, shortest covering</a>.</p>\r\n"
  },
